  "result": "Excellent! The discount feature is fully implemented and all 98 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **Error handling**: Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error to `src/errors.js` for invalid discount values\n\n2. **Discount validation**: Created `isValidDiscount()` function that accepts values from 0-100 (including decimals like 12.5), returns `true` for undefined/null (defaults to 0), and rejects negative, >100, or non-numeric values\n\n3. **createInvoice enhancement**: \n   - Now accepts optional `discountPercent` on line items\n   - Validates and stores `discountPercent` on each line (defaults to 0)\n\n4. **addLine enhancement**:\n   - Now accepts optional `discountPercent` when adding lines\n   - Validates and stores it (defaults to 0)\n\n5. **invoiceTotals restructure**:\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` instead of just `{ subtotal, total }`\n   - Calculates line discount as: `lineTotal \u00d7 (discountPercent / 100)`\n   - Sums all line discounts for the invoice discount\n   - Total is `subtotal - discount`\n   - All amounts clamped at 0 (no negative values)\n\n6. **Comprehensive test coverage**: Added 16 new tests covering decimal discounts, validation errors, single/multiple line discounts, and zero-clamping\n\nThe implementation handles edge cases correctly:\n- Decimal percentages (12.5% works perfectly)\n- 100% discount reduces total to 0\n- Mixed discounted and non-discounted lines\n- Proper validation rejecting out-of-range or invalid types",
